      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},$ then $\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-20\\pi )=$",
      "worked_solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-10$ into the right-hand-side gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-20\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},$ then $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-20\\pi )=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-20\\pi )=\\sqrt{5}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$",
